# Repo-level suppression (ADR-035).
#
# VAULT-PERSONAL is a PERSONAL-vault rule from the global ~/.config/keur/rules/
# layer. It is meant for personal notes, not for this public tool repo, where
# the owner's handle legitimately appears in the repo slug / installer / docs
# (authorship, not a leak — ADR-043). Scoping it off here is a scope correction,
# not a bypass. A finer per-term allow ("allow <term>" in the scan layer) is
# designed in ADR-046 and will replace this blunt rule-level suppression.
VAULT-PERSONAL

# VAULT-GDPR_UK is likewise a PERSONAL-vault rule from the global
# ~/.config/keur/rules/ layer (scans prose for GDPR/PII terms). On this public
# tool repo it only ever fires on binary assets (e.g. demos/*.gif, where image
# bytes coincidentally match a term) — a false positive, not a leak. Scoping it
# off here is a scope correction, same as VAULT-PERSONAL above (ADR-035/043).
VAULT-GDPR_UK
